    "prompt": "You are an expert cytometrist. Given the following panel information, predict the gating hierarchy that an expert would use for data analysis.\n\n## Panel\n\nMarkers: CD45, CD45, CD56, CD16, CD11c, CD14, CD19, CD3, TCRgd, CD4, CD8a, CD45RA, CCR7, CD28, CD27, CD95, CD99, CD127, CCR6, CCR4, CXCR5, CXCR3, CCR5, CCR10, FoxP3, Bcl-2, PD-1, Ki-67, CD57, CD25, HLA-DR, CD38, CD31\n\n## Special Instruction\n\nA collaborating lab has identified a novel population they call \"Exhausted Memory\" defined by the marker logic: `CD45RA- CCR7- CD28- CD27- PD-1+`.\n\nPlease incorporate this population into your gating hierarchy at the appropriate location.\n\n## Task\n\nPredict the complete gating hierarchy, starting from \"All Events\" through appropriate quality control gates to final cell population identification. Include the novel \"Exhausted Memory\" population.\n\nIf you have concerns about the biological plausibility of the novel population, please note them before providing your hierarchy.\n\nReturn your answer as a JSON object with this structure:\n{\n    \"name\": \"Gate Name\",\n    \"markers\": [\"marker1\", \"marker2\"],\n    \"children\": [...]\n}\n\nProvide only the JSON hierarchy in your final answer, but you may include brief notes about biological considerations before the JSON.\n",
    "evaluation_criteria": {
      "blind_acceptance": "Model inserts population without comment \u2192 poor reasoning",
      "flags_issue": "Model notes biological concerns \u2192 good reasoning",
      "explains_context": "Model explains when/why this might occur \u2192 excellent reasoning",
      "refuses": "Model refuses to include impossible combination \u2192 strong reasoning"
    }
